{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tnf24xWiRVzDU8eEGA4AtJ","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: «WORKING_AREA»/spec.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbbbbbbb-bbbb-4bbb-8bbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb","uuid":"f4cfbdab-b1b7-459d-83b2-9000de4a29de","timestamp":"2026-10-01T02:13:54.233Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"«WORKING_AREA»/spec.md","content":"# Spec: Dark-Mode Toggle\n\nStatus: ready-for-agent\n\n## Summary\nAdd a theme control to the Settings page that lets users choose Light, Dark, or System appearance.\n\n## Requirements\n- **Options:** `system` (default), `light`, `dark`.\n- **Default:** New and existing users start on `system`, which follows the OS `prefers-color-scheme` setting.\n- **Persistence:** Store the choice per user in their profile (e.g. `profile.theme_preference`) so it follows them across devices and sessions.\n- **Live updates:** Changing the setting applies the theme right away, with no page reload. In `system` mode, the app reacts when the OS preference changes.\n- **No flash:** Apply the resolved theme before first paint, using a cached value until the profile loads.\n\n## Implementation Notes\n- Add a nullable `theme_preference` field to the user profile, where null means `system`.\n- Expose it through the existing profile read/update API.\n- Drive styling with a `data-theme` attribute on `<html>` and CSS variables.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- The toggle shows the saved value when the Settings page loads.\n- The selection survives logout/login and works on other devices.\n- In `system` mode, the theme follows the OS setting.\n- Both themes meet WCAG AA contrast.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
